sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Wealth user
    participant W as Next.js page /customers/[id]
    participant Q as TanStack Query cache
    participant R as Router portfolio.py
    participant D as deps (CurrentUser)
    participant S as PortfolioService
    participant P as PortfolioRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    U->>W: open customer C0026, Portfolio tab
    W->>Q: useQuery(["portfolio","C0026"])
    Q->>R: GET /api/v1/customers/C0026/portfolio (cookie)
    R->>R: path regex ^C\d{4,}$ (422 otherwise)
    R->>D: decode JWT, SELECT users WHERE id = :sub
    D-->>R: active user (any role)
    R->>S: for_customer("C0026")
    S->>DB: SELECT EXISTS(customer) - 404 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if absent
    S->>P: accounts(customer)
    P->>DB: SELECT ... FROM accounts WHERE customer_id = :id
    S->>P: latest_snapshot_date()
    P->>DB: SELECT max(snapshot_date) FROM holdings_snapshot (PK index)
    S->>P: aggregates(customer, date)
    P->>DB: v_position_valuation ... GROUP BY GROUPING SETS ((account_id),(asset_class),())
    DB-->>P: account rows + asset-class rows + total row (NUMERIC)
    S->>P: positions(customer, date)
    P->>DB: v_position_valuation + sum(market_value) OVER () for weight_pct
    DB-->>P: positions ordered by market_value DESC
    S->>S: merge: every account listed (zero if no positions),<br/>allocation sorted, freshness {snapshot_date, price_as_of, stale_prices}
    S-->>R: Portfolio model
    R-->>Q: 200 JSON, money rounded half-up to 2 dp at serialisation
    Q-->>W: cached (staleTime), render totals, account cards,<br/>allocation chart + table fallback, positions table
    Note over S,DB: 5 queries, constant per customer (no N+1). All money maths in NUMERIC inside PostgreSQL.